Issue #12 item N1 -- mutation evidence for the /live/hls/ nginx location
================================================================================

Setup: docker/scripts/patch_pkg_location.py then docker/scripts/
patch_live_hls_location.py (both from frigate-vulkan) applied in sequence to
a scratch copy of corvette's own tests/nginx-parity/vendor/nginx.conf, then
tests/nginx-parity/offline.patch applied on top for unprivileged local
execution (stub upstream ports, non-root paths) -- exactly the chain the
real Dockerfile.py313 build runs, plus the same unprivileged adaptation
corvette's own nginx-parity harness already uses. A real nginx 1.30.4 (from
'nix develop') serves this config; a plain Python HTTP server on
127.0.0.1:8556 (stub_hls_backend.py) stands in for G3's own HLS listener,
answering exactly its documented contract (GET /<camera>/playlist.m3u8 ->
application/vnd.apple.mpegurl, GET /<camera>/init.mp4 and
/<camera>/segment-<n>.m4s -> video/mp4); a stub Frigate /auth (202) and a
stub go2rtc player page fill the other two upstreams every proxied location
in this file needs. scripts/route_parity.sh (issue #12 INV-4) is the actual
assertion harness: three new rows for /live/hls/front_door/{playlist.m3u8,
init.mp4,segment-0.m4s}, each asserting status, content type, AND a body
predicate that is absent from this site's own SPA shell (absent:id="root"),
so a silent fallback to the shell (this file's known 200-with-wrong-body
failure mode) cannot pass by accident.

Command (both runs):
  bash scripts/route_parity.sh --table n1-route-rows.table --mode local \
    --base-url http://127.0.0.1:18980

--- BROKEN (location /live/hls/ { ... } removed from the patched nginx.conf) -- FAIL ---

  FAIL /live/hls/front_door/playlist.m3u8: content-type 'text/html', expected 'application/vnd.apple.mpegurl'
  FAIL /live/hls/front_door/init.mp4: content-type 'text/html', expected 'video/mp4'
  FAIL /live/hls/front_door/segment-0.m4s: content-type 'text/html', expected 'video/mp4'
route_parity: 3/3 rows checked, 3 failed
exit code: 1

Confirms the defect: with the location block removed, /live/hls/* falls
through to nginx's own SPA-fallback location / (try_files ... /index.html),
which answers 200 text/html carrying the donor shell -- exactly the
silent wrong-body failure mode INV-4 exists to catch. A status-code-only
check would have missed this entirely (both the broken and working
responses are HTTP 200).

--- AFTER RESTORE (location /live/hls/ { ... } restored verbatim) -- PASS ---

  ok   /live/hls/front_door/playlist.m3u8: 200 application/vnd.apple.mpegurl
  ok   /live/hls/front_door/init.mp4: 200 video/mp4
  ok   /live/hls/front_door/segment-0.m4s: 200 video/mp4
route_parity: 3/3 rows checked, 0 failed
exit code: 0

Confirms the fix: restoring the exact removed block returns /live/hls/*
to proxying at G3's own stub listener, and all three rows pass again --
same table, same base URL, only the location block's presence differs
between this run and the BROKEN one above.

--- Donor-drift guard (patch_live_hls_location.py's own md5 check) ---

Check 1: fresh vendored nginx.conf -> patch_pkg_location.py -> patch_live_hls_location.py (correct chained order) -- PASS
  $ python3 patch_pkg_location.py nginx.conf && python3 patch_live_hls_location.py nginx.conf
  patch_pkg_location: /pkg/ location inserted
  patch_live_hls_location: /live/hls/ location inserted
  exit code: 0

Check 2: a stale donor copy -- patch_pkg_location.py never run -- fed directly to
patch_live_hls_location.py (the exact scenario this guard exists to catch: this
script assumes it runs SECOND in the Dockerfile, after the /pkg/ patch, so its
own EXPECTED_MD5 is the POST-/pkg/-patch md5, not the pristine donor's) -- FAIL
patch_live_hls_location: /tmp/drift-fail.conf is md5 ab5dc3e90e54616dc30c7cdc8fac4048, but the expected input (donor nginx.conf from Frigate 3d4dd3ac4/v0.17.2, with patch_pkg_location.py's /pkg/ location already applied) is 99c599fe0c13ff3efd6a5a35d49042a1 -- either FRIGATE_IMAGE has drifted from the revision this patch was written against, or this script no longer runs immediately after patch_pkg_location.py in the Dockerfile. Re-verify both insertion points by hand, update EXPECTED_MD5 here (and patch_pkg_location.py's own EXPECTED_MD5 plus tests/nginx-parity/vendor/PROVENANCE in corvette, if the donor itself changed) together, then retry.
exit code: 1

Confirms the guard: check 1 (correct chain order) passes; check 2 (this
script fed the wrong input -- the pristine donor instead of patch_pkg_location.py's
own output) fails loudly on the md5 mismatch rather than silently inserting
this item's hunk at an unverified anchor.

Restore verified byte-for-byte, not just visually
--------------------------------------------------
After the AFTER RESTORE run above, the harness's own nginx.conf (with
offline.patch's unprivileged-run edits reversed back out via `patch -R`) was
diffed against a completely fresh `patch_pkg_location.py` + `patch_live_hls_location.py`
application to the pristine vendored donor:

    $ diff fresh-two-scripts-applied.conf restored-harness-minus-offline-patch.conf
    Files are identical

Confirms the restore was exact -- not a block that merely looks the same, but
the identical bytes a clean chained run of both production patch scripts
would produce.

Cleanup
-------
All local harness processes (the two nginx instances and the Python HLS
stand-in) were stopped and their listening ports (15001, 15002, 8556, 18980,
15020) confirmed free afterward. The harness itself lived entirely under this
session's scratchpad directory, not under `corvette` or `frigate-vulkan`; the
only frigate-vulkan changes are `docker/scripts/patch_live_hls_location.py`
(new) and `docker/Dockerfile.py313` (chains it after `patch_pkg_location.py`),
and the only corvette change beyond this evidence file is three new rows
appended to `tests/route-parity/expectations` -- both left uncommitted,
proposed for human review together with this evidence.
